 "capability": "genetic-ancestry",
 "title": "Genetic ancestry per donor",
 "conclusion": "On 150 1000 Genomes individuals from 26 populations (MAGE RNA-seq thinned to single-cell donor depth, leave-out reference), Singlet's published ancestry label is correct for 86.0% at 8m read pairs, against 92.0% for somalier, 99.3% for peddy.",
 "methods": "Truth: 150 individuals of the 1000 Genomes Project, 30 per super-population and sex-balanced, covering all 26 populations, whose lymphoblastoid lines were RNA-sequenced by MAGE (Taylor et al. 2024, PRJNA851328). The first 8M read pairs of each run were aligned once with STAR 2.7.11b to GRCh38-2024-A, then thinned to 2M and 0.5M pairs. Every tool reads the same alignments at each depth. Singlet: singlet.celllabels.ancestry, supervised admixture with fixed super-population allele frequencies at the pipeline's 1000 Genomes SNP panel. Its depth tables come from bcftools mpileup (MAPQ 255, BQ 20). The frequencies were recomputed without the 154 test individuals, so no tool sees its own answer. The published label is the super-population with proportion q >= 0.8, otherwise 'admixed'. somalier 0.3.6: extract at its hg38 sites, then ancestry against the labelled 1000 Genomes background minus the test individuals. peddy 0.4.8: bcftools call at its GRCh38 sites, then peddy with its built-in 1000 Genomes background minus the test individuals (peddy_leaveout.py). Metrics: accuracy of each tool's published label (an abstention counts as wrong), accuracy of the most likely super-population, and precision of named calls, with 95% Wilson intervals. Donor sex: Singlet's sex model on the sample's XIST and chrY gene counts, against peddy's sex check and the XIST/chrY rule.",
 "status": "draft",
 "generated_at": "2026-10-26T11:20:28+00:00",
 "owner": "bench-public",
