 "caveats": [
  "Bulk RNA-seq of cell lines stands in for single-cell donors: reads are thinned to 0.5M-8M pairs, the range of a donor's coverage in a single-cell library, but full-length bulk coverage spreads over more sites than 3' single-cell reads.",
  "Depth tables come from bcftools mpileup on STAR alignments (MAPQ 255, BQ 20), the same input for every tool, not from Singlet's own pileup engine; the end-to-end single-cell runs are scored separately.",
  "Bulk donor sex: Singlet's per-cell model calls 15 of 150 MAGE individuals ambiguous (female by 1000 Genomes). Bulk RNA of these cell lines carries both XIST and reads on chrY genes with X homologs, which the single-cell model treats as a doublet signature; the XIST/chrY rule fails on bulk for the same reason. Single-cell results are in chromosomal-sex."
 ]
